        "original_id": "329add56-2db5-5028-ac0b-bc56f389ecdd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Susanna Thompson, Rob Reiner, Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, James Woods, Stephen Amell, Willa Holland, David Ramsey, Colin Donnell, Katie Cassidy, Paul Blackthorne\n- Works: Little Giants, Ghosts of Mississippi, Random Hearts, Dragonfly, Once and Again, Arrow, Pilot (Arrow)\n- Roles: Karen Sammler, Moira Queen, Oliver Queen, Thea, John Diggle, Tommy Merlyn, Laurel Lance, Quentin Lance\n- Organizations: ABC\n\nFacts:\n- Susanna Thompson was born on January 27, 1958, and is an American actress.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Little Giants in 1994.\n- Ghosts of Mississippi is a 1996 American biographical courtroom drama film directed by Rob Reiner and starring Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, and James Woods.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Ghosts of Mississippi in 1996.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Random Hearts in 1999.\n- Susanna Thompson played Karen Sammler on the ABC drama series Once and Again from 1999 to 2002.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Dragonfly in 2002.\n- The Pilot episode of Arrow introduces Oliver Queen, played by Stephen Amell, as well as Moira Queen, played by Susanna Thompson, Thea, played by Willa Holland, John Diggle, played by David Ramsey, Tommy Merlyn, played by Colin Donnell, Laurel Lance, played by Katie Cassidy, and Detective Quentin Lance, played by Paul Blackthorne.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
